    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the trio of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (71.77), and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlines our offense, as he faces a favorable matchup against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez; the combination of the pitcher\u2019s 4.32 xERA and a significant dynamic platoon edge (+14%) makes him our most efficient start. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** similarly benefits from his projected spot in the order and a favorable platoon profile against the lefty Quinn Mathews. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** grades out as a high-upside play due to a substantial park factor boost (+10%), which elevates his raw production ceiling despite a reasonably competent opposing starter.\n\nStrategic considerations for today include the difficult decision to leave **Gunnar Henderson** on the bench. Despite his immense talent, **Gunnar Henderson** sits at a 52.11 score because he is facing a sub-3.00 xERA arm in Cristopher S\u00e1nchez, and the cumulative impact of an elite opposing catcher's hold rate on stolen base attempts significantly suppressed his utility in our SB-sensitive league. Furthermore, we are closely monitoring the rain risk (37%) impacting the games involving **Drake Baldwin**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Dominic Smith**. Should the weather force a postponement in those matchups, we will look to re-evaluate the bench, though for now, **Drake Baldwin** remains a strong play (68.78) purely on the strength of his secondary metrics against the pitcher.\n\nLastly, while **Kyle Tucker** (54.86) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (57.22) project slightly lower than our top tier, they remain locked into the starting lineup due to the scarcity of high-speed, high-impact contributors. We have opted to prioritize **Jackson Merrill** (68.55) in the outfield over alternative bench options, as he effectively navigated the risks posed by his matchup despite a negative modifier for catcher throw-out efficiency. We will continue to track the official lineups for **Drake Baldwin**, **Liam Hicks**, and the rest of the squad to ensure our assumed batting positions hold true, as any significant drop in order placement could force a late-afternoon rotation shift for the bench-heavy bats like **Coby Mayo** or **Sam Antonacci**.",
